<title>UK: UK to increase spending on health next year.</title>
<headline>UK to increase spending on health next year.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said Britain will increase spending on patient services by 1.6 billion stg next year in real terms.</p>
<p>&quot;For next year we will increase current spending on patient services by 1.6 billion stg, or 2.9 percent in real terms,&quot; Clarke told parliament in his annual budget speech.</p>
<p>&quot;The real increase in current spending for hospitals next year over and above inflation will be three percent.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
